@page "/docs/components/toast"

<DocsPage Title="Toast" Description="A succinct message that is displayed temporarily.">
    <ComponentPreview Name="toast-demo" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Installation" />
    <InstallationTabs Name="toast">
        <Setup>
            <Step>Register a <code>ToastManager</code> for each user.</Step>
            <CodeFigure Code="@ProgramCode" Language="csharp" Title="Program.cs" LineNumbers="true" Highlight="@([3])" />
            <Step>Add the <code>Toaster</code> component.</Step>
            <CodeFigure Code="@LayoutCode" Title="Components/Layout/MainLayout.razor" LineNumbers="true" Highlight="@([4])" />
        </Setup>
    </InstallationTabs>
    <DocsHeading Title="Usage" />
    <p>Inject the <code>ToastManager</code> and add toasts to it. The <code>Toaster</code> in your layout shows them.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@UsageCode" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Types" />
    <p>Set the <code>Type</code> option to render a status icon. The built-in renderer recognizes <code>success</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>error</code>, and <code>loading</code>.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="toast-types" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Action" />
    <p>Set <code>ActionLabel</code> and <code>OnAction</code> to render an action button. The toast closes after the action runs.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ActionCode" Language="csharp" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Promise" />
    <p>Use <code>ToastManager.Promise</code> to update one toast as an asynchronous task moves through loading, success, and error states.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="toast-promise" />
    <DocsHeading Title="API Reference" />
    <ApiReference Name="toast" />
</DocsPage>

@code {
    private const string ProgramCode = """
        builder.Services.AddRazorComponents().AddInteractiveServerComponents();

        builder.Services.AddScoped<ToastManager>();
        """;

    private const string LayoutCode = """
        @inherits LayoutComponentBase

        <main>@Body</main>
        <Toaster />
        """;

    private const string UsageCode = """
        @inject ToastManager Toasts

        <Button @onclick="Notify">Show Toast</Button>

        @code {
            private void Notify() =>
                Toasts.Add(new ToastOptions
                {
                    Title = "Event created",
                    Description = "Sunday, December 3 at 9:00 AM",
                });
        }
        """;

    private const string ActionCode = """
        Toasts.Add(new ToastOptions
        {
            Title = "Event created",
            ActionLabel = "Undo",
            OnAction = UndoAsync,
        });
        """;
}
